<title>BELGIUM: Sabca to supply Airbus brake parts.</title>
<headline>Sabca to supply Airbus brake parts.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian aerospace company Sabca said on Friday it had won a contract with French aerospace company Messier-Bugatti to supply brake parts for Airbus A320 aircraft.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>In a statement, Sabca said the brake parts it would supply were a spin-off from its work for the Ariane rocket programme. &quot;This contract confirms the willingness of Sabca to extend its activity into civil (aviation) applications,&quot; Sabca said.</p>
<p>The contract was signed at France's Le Bourget airshow.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
